  "worked_solution": "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-(-7))^{2}}{{10}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-(-3))^{2}}{{8}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h=-3$ and $k=-7.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,-3,-7\\,).$",
